      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Would be great to have a \"proportional movement speed\" toggle on the expressions menu now that we have avatar scaling built in to the game, where if you shrink below default you can optionally move slower. Perhaps there can be a cap to the maximum speed if there's a concern that going faster than default would cause issues with cheating in a game world, or the max and min speeds could be defined by world authors.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-06-10T23:20:49.665Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I think it'd be quite nice to have different settable movement speeds that scale with the size of the model. I have a few 5 meter models that run like a chicken with no head, so it looks quite awkward. It'd be extreamly cool if the bigger the model, the slower the \"move animation\" was, but it was faster to move. That way bigger models could look like they're moving proper instead of running 500Mph in one spot.",
